# PCExhumed
===
PCExhumed is an accurate source port of the PC release of Exhumed (known in North America as PowerSlave), the 1996 Egyptian-themed first-person shooter. Based on the EDuke32 BUILD engine, it provides native 64-bit performance on Linux.

Features:
- Native execution on modern operating systems with high-resolution widescreen rendering
- Smooth mouselook controls with customizable keybindings and crosshairs
- Full support for original game data, CD audio soundtracks, and voiceovers
- Enhanced dynamic lighting, particle effects, and uncapped framerate options
- Restores cut features and fixes engine glitches present in the original DOS release
